WEBVTT

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.980
<i>Time that has passed can never return.</i>

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:06.980
Time Can Never Return

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.280
<i>But, even if all is lost,</i>

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:12.280
Even if All Is Lost

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.930
<i>there will still be a future.</i>

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:16.450
There Will Still Be a Future.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.720
February 14    23:45

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.280
Whose time are you trying to devour now?

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.040
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.570
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.600
I'll be taking back the time

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.460
that you stole from us.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.510
February 15    16:30

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.510
No, it's true!

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:06.320
If you make a wish under the clock 
tower at the Central Cemetery,

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.730
you can turn back time!

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.360
That's just an urban legend, isn't it?

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:12.600
I'd love to turn back time.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.620
I've gained weight lately.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.100
I wonder if I could get 
back with my ex-boyfriend.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.780
Come on, that can't really be true.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:23.230
Jeez, Koyuki, why do you have 
to say things like that?

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.290
Have you no sense of romanticism?

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.870
Of course I do, but seriously,

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.870
you know it's not possible to turn back time.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:34.250
We know, but it doesn't 
hurt to dream a little!

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.140
Dreams are fine,

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.800
but right now, we need to work
on our graduation surprise. Right?

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.680
We'll be singing for our 
families and teachers.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.760
Leave the accompaniment to me.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.500
Wow... It's all worked out.
Even the program and our positions!

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.940
You're good, Koyuki!

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.730
Let's all work hard.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.190
We need to express our gratitude to 
the people who are precious to us.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.460
My father's going to cry when he hears this.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:08.330
And I bet my brother will be so 
overwhelmed that he cries his eyes out!

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.920
I'll go let Ms. Emily know.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.560
Hey, isn't Koyuki's brother...

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.600
Yeah. They were the only two 
members of their family.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.890
Ms. Emily.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.400
Everyone's talking about how you 
suddenly look much younger these days.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.370
Even the head office 
wouldn't recognize you now.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:45.950
Have you performed some 
sort of magic recently?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.620
Perhaps what they call
"turning back time," for example?

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.290
Please refrain from speaking of matters 
unrelated to work, Vice Principal.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.510
Oh, dear. My apologies.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.770
Do you need something, Koyuki?

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.050
Yes, actually.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:12.060
But you know, she should 
want to turn back time

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.150
more than any of us.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.480
Brother...

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.040
Are you all alone, too?

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.080
You know, I once had an older brother.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:45.210
But... he's gone now.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.820
Koyuki!

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:54.690
Brother!

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.770
Oh, my violin!

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.380
Koyuki!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.110
It was all...

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.880
...my fault.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.930
If only the legend about 
the clock tower were true.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.930
Then I could see you again, and...

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.950
Wh-What? What was that?

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:51.250
You can't run.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:51.950
Huh?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.250
What is this thing?

00:05:58.380 --> 00:05:59.710
A monster?

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.420
What's that? A katana?

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.180
If you think you've escaped, 
you're gravely mistaken.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.750
Victor is waiting just up ahead.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:15.180
Any moment now, I'll hear your dying screams.

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:20.440
Any moment now, I'll hear your dying screams.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.730
Any moment now—

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:25.620
Um...

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.650
Aw, leaving already?

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.990
Stay a little longer, Victor!

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.370
I can't do that.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.620
Promise you'll come again, okay?

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:35.780
Sure.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.800
And if I break my promise,

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.160
Kiri over there...

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:42.960
will eat pasta through his nose.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:44.960
Why me?!

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:49.180
Our plan was to use a pincer attack!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.110
Why are you goofing around here?

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.390
What if that Horologue was the one
we're seeking vengeance against?!

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:55.390
Kiri...

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:59.770
Stiffs like you have no 
chance of ever getting married.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.880
There's no way a prime 
specimen like me won't—

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.270
Wait, forget that, Victor!

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.830
Are you aware of the position you're in?!

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:08.930
Behind you.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.010
Don't change the subject!

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.110
Um...

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.930
You're... Koyuki, right?

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:38.640
We're, um... actors, you see.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:45.310
We're here to film a movie,
and what you saw before was just...

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.160
A special effect!

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:50.820
An elite H*llywood film crew was
milling around behind us.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:52.780
They've all left by now, though.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.010
You're an actor, Victor?

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:56.950
You said before that you 
were a bounty hunter.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.110
I-It's a movie about a bounty hunter!

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:01.330
Oh, I see!

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:06.680
Victor Putin's journal, February 15th.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:10.260
My brother, Kiri Putin, just lied 
for the first time in his life.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:11.950
His acting sucks,

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:16.520
but his first step toward breaking free of 
his serious nature must be commemorated.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.720
You piece of...

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:21.110
Well, I can't help it.

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:24.100
I forget things if I don't 
write them in my journal.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.590
Actors? Your brother?

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.480
What's really the truth here?

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.440
The truth is always within 
your heart, my lady.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.530
Cut it out, you lecherous geezer!

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.030
Was "geezer" really necessary?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.000
At least call me a lecherous young man
 or an erotic boy or something!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.580
That is true.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.700
"Geezer" is perfectly appropriate for him!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:48.000
Despite his looks, he's a 
geezer right to the core!

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.750
That's also true.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.340
It's so nice to have a brother.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.640
I envy you.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:02.060
If only the legend about 
the clock tower were true,

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.770
my brother would also...

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.040
You believe in that nonsense?

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.770
Those who have died can never return.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.020
That—

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.790
Hey, that was harsh!

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.110
Wasn't there some other way to say that?

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.960
I'll tell you the truth.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.160
The legend about the clock tower is true.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:21.620
Many people have used its power 
to travel back to the past.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.540
Yes, in fact, we are—

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:32.250
Victor, my dear brother,
look at the time! We must go!

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:34.780
Well, thank you, ladies!

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:37.310
And Koyuki, forget about your brother!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:39.370
Don't think about him! Understand?

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:40.630
Farewell!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.040
For the love of...

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:56.610
Are you a child?!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.530
I'm Victor Putin, five years old 
and prettier than a flower!

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:02.190
And it wasn't just today!

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:04.330
How many times must you hold me back?

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:06.560
Are you doing this on purpose?!

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:08.710
Perhaps.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.080
What?!

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:13.840
You even tried to tell Koyuki the 
truth about the legend, didn't you?

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.620
What if she had really believed you?

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.760
Haven't you been more affected than anyone

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.620
by the fact that the only 
thing that attracts Horologues

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.470
is the desire born from human regret?

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:27.980
So if you look at it differently, isn't this
really a chance to attract Horologues?

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:33.570
It's too late once that girl
is exposed to danger!

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:38.250
Kiri, you think that if we
warn her in the strongest terms,

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.070
we can change her mind, don't you?

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:46.620
But someone won't stop thinking
just because you said they must,

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.440
nor will they forget just because
they were told they must.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.790
It's not that simple.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.860
I'm willing to bet on it.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.120
If we don't force reality upon that girl,

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.340
it'll be impossible to erase her desire.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:02.540
Reality...

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:13.860
March 1    10:28

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.340
As we graduate today,
we'd like to express our gratitude

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:13.540
to all of you with this song.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:51.210
<i>All of my friends' parents, and all 
of our teachers, were overjoyed.</i>

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.000
<i>So were you, right, Brother?</i>

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:06.860
I'll tell you the truth.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.190
The legend about the clock tower is true.

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:15.470
The address on the card 
should be around here.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.230
Ms. Emily?

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.510
It couldn't be.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.900
That legend really is true, isn't it,

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:39.590
Victor?!

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:43.570
Victor Putin's journal, March 1st.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.740
The foolish little girl gave in to 
temptation and came straight to me.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:51.250
Tell me the truth about the legend!

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:56.200
If you make a wish under the clock tower 
at midnight on the night of a full moon,

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.960
time will be turned back.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:03.840
Care to try it?

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:07.090
Make time...

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.100
turn back!

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:16.060
Turn it back to when my 
brother was still alive!

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:35.370
Time... Give me time.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.380
<i>Even so,</i>

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:40.380
<i>I want</i>

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.500
<i>my brother</i>

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.380
<i>to come back to me!</i>

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:00.680
Kiri?

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:01.920
You...

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:05.410
idiot!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.410
How many times must I tell you not 
to involve ordinary citizens in this?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.640
What do you think would have happened 
if I hadn't gotten here in time?!

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.270
I wouldn't have landed on my butt.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:19.420
Do you even know the meaning 
of the word "remorse"?!

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:21.630
Stay back, Koyuki.

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:26.220
Koyuki!

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.300
Don't stop me!

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:31.260
You guys don't understand my pain!

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.850
Because both of you brothers are alive!

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.900
If it'll bring my brother back to life,

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:39.600
I don't care if that thing 
is a demon or anything else!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:41.700
Didn't I tell you?

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:45.010
Human desire is not so easily erased.

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.360
Give it back...

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:54.410
Give my time back to me!

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.160
Ms. Emily?

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.210
No! Get away from that!

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.710
Time...

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.250
This is the truth of the legend.

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:23.770
These things are demons called Horologues.

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:28.110
They appear to grant the wishes of 
people who want to return to the past,

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:32.270
but in truth, they're only
eating humans' time.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:34.790
When a human is bitten by a Horologue,

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:37.380
their time is drained away,
and they return to nothingness.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:40.830
This is what it means to 
make a contract with them.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:47.880
Victor!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.600
Oath of Time, activate!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:01.190
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:01.190
Slow Down!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.870
Time stopped.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.840
No, to be precise, I didn't stop it.

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:25.930
Victor is only using the cards

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:29.390
to reduce an object's passage
through time to its slowest possible speed.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.050
Just what are you guys?

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.050
We control time using this, the Oath of Time,

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:40.060
to battle the Horologues,
demons that devour humans' time.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.610
We are Chronos Rulers.

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:49.190
Chronos Rulers?

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:53.970
But all we can really control 
is the speed of time.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:57.750
We can't know the future 
or return to the past.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:58.990
Give up on your brother.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.750
I can't give up on him!

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:04.120
He was the only family I had, and I lost him!

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:07.230
Do you have any idea how 
I feel?! You can't—

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:07.920
We do.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.550
Victor let our mother die.

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:16.320
In his regret, he wished to change the past.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.870
His regret brought a Horologue to us.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.170
Take a good look.

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:24.230
This is what true loss looks like.

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:30.230
The Oath of Time stops the flow of 
Victor's own time from within him.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.690
It was the only way.

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.650
Being bitten by a Horologue

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:38.480
doesn't just make you younger.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:39.950
Your memories disappear, too.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.120
There's so much I don't remember anymore.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:45.230
No...

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:51.380
Oath of Time, activate!

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:50.130
<b>Oath</b>

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:00.070
Kiri, you protect Koyuki

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:01.570
with that Teenage Fantasy Sword of yours!

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:03.220
Don't call it weird names!

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:08.010
Slow Down!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:08.520
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:13.820
Slow Down!

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:14.440
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:31.840
Victor!

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:35.880
You're stronger than I thought.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.720
That's the way!

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.010
Why?

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.470
He's so badly hurt.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:48.330
We may be able to control time,

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:51.440
but what happened in the 
past cannot be changed.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:54.930
What's important is how much 
you cared for each other

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:59.320
and strengthened the bond you had 
during the time you lived together.

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:02.410
Now, then...

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.930
There's no skill in just trying to get away.

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:08.370
It's time for my counterattack.

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:09.670
Don't, Victor!

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:12.790
Whoa, Kiri. Your job is to protect Koyuki.

00:19:12.990 --> 00:19:14.510
Leave this to me.

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:18.740
After all, I promised Mom 
that I'd protect you.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.630
It's written in my journal.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.220
No! Don't do it!

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.720
What's going on?

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:26.660
When he uses Speed Up,

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:29.260
the flow of Victor's time 
from within him accelerates.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:30.730
That means...

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:36.190
He's about to give up his own 
time in return for our safety.

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:39.760
I thought that if I lost my memories,

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.870
I would eventually stop feeling 
the pain in my heart, as well.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:46.300
But don't worry.

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:48.040
It's still very painful.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:54.530
In return, I'll let you experience 
what it feels like to be alive,

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:57.170
with a card that can fire at Mach 10!

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.670
Victor...

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:06.430
Speed Up!

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.110
Ace Shot!

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:40.550
Where am I?

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:41.740
Victor!

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:43.650
Huh?

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:45.840
What the heck happened?

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:46.850
It's me, Kiri.

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:49.090
Victor, do you recognize me?

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:50.280
Kiri?

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:56.020
Here, eat this pasta through your nose.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.230
That's what you start with?!

00:20:57.410 --> 00:21:00.660
Huh? The pasta's all crusty.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:03.290
<i>Thank goodness. He hasn't 
lost that much time.</i>

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.450
Eating this through your nose 
would give you a nosebleed.

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:07.870
Actually, did you already eat 
your pasta through your nose?

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:10.490
Huh? Er, I... uh...

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.370
Y-Yeah, I did!

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:14.620
What, really? Are you serious?

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.500
Yeah, I'm serious! And it 
was seriously al dente!

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:22.510
I think you dropped this.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:25.770
Look at the back of the photo.

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:26.720
The back?

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:34.890
Always...

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:39.400
<i>I'll always be by your side, Koyuki.</i>

00:21:55.820 --> 00:21:57.180
Brother...

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:03.260
Koyuki, your brother is 
no longer in this world,

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:06.680
but you haven't lost the memories of 
the time you had with him, have you?

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:10.160
That in itself is a priceless treasure.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:14.280
Yeah.

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:54.220
Come to think of it...

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:57.100
What is Victor's actual age?

00:22:57.590 --> 00:23:00.450
He becomes one day younger 
with each passing day,

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:02.110
and his memories are lost at the same time.

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:06.360
So does that mean Victor is 
actually the older brother?

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:13.180
<i>Victor Putin. True age: 39.</i>

00:23:13.180 --> 00:23:14.370
<i>My...</i>

00:23:16.280 --> 00:23:17.410
<i>father.</i>

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:24.750
Being and Nothingness

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:40.250
Memory and Reminiscence
